// A part rendered ONLY as tablature, carrying its own (6-sharp) key, beside a concert
// notation staff. A tab staff ENGRAVES no key signature — LilyPond's TabStaff removes the
// Key_engraver (ly/engraver-init.ly:1214) — so that key must reserve NOTHING. Before the
// fix the reservation walked every staff while the drawing walk skipped tab/text/ossia, so
// it booked a key column nobody draws and left a 7.05 ss hole between the meter and the
// first note (ledger line-start.time-to-first-note.tab-keyed, probe scores TKC/TKT, whose
// two LilyPond twins are geometrically identical).
title "Tab Part Key"

octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major

part gt { clef treble }
part pn { clef treble }

section Main {
  gt { key fis major  c,4 d, e, f, | g,2 e, }
  pn { c4 d e f | g2 e }
}

form main { Main }

score main "tab-part-key" {
  staff pn
  tab gt
}
